Design notes:
- Operation depends on a narrow _Resumer protocol (handler_for, is_local,
  schedule_local) rather than on Client, so the two modules do not import each
  other and the async client can satisfy the same shape.
- The path is validated before anything is scheduled. A task pointing at an
  unregistered path would be dispatched, fail, and retry until the queue gave up.
- Local timers are bounded by TASK_DEADLINE so a handler cannot be given more
  time locally than Cloud Tasks would allow in production, are daemon threads so
  they cannot hold up interpreter exit, and are held in a set so close() can
  cancel them and the GC cannot collect a pending resume.
- Logging goes through the stdlib 'alis.build.lro' logger. Go's lro imports
  go.alis.build/alog; product principle 4 forbids depending on a sibling package,
  and a service that installs alis-build-alog still gets structured output.
